@startuml
title S8  Authorize each personal request  US-15
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontColor #172A3A
skinparam defaultFontSize 15
skinparam ArrowColor #345A72
skinparam Shadowing false
skinparam dpi 150
skinparam TitleFontColor #123A52
skinparam TitleFontSize 19
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor #EDF5FA
skinparam ClassBorderColor #456F89
skinparam ComponentBackgroundColor #EDF5FA
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #456F89
skinparam PackageBorderColor #456F89
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #E6F4F0
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #417364
skinparam SequenceGroupBackgroundColor #EDF5FA
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor #617C8D
hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam maxMessageSize 220
actor User
participant "Web UI" as UI
participant "Protected routes" as API

participant JwtGuard as Guard
participant "tokens: TokenService" as Token
User -> UI : request a personal action
UI -> API : personal request with bearer JWT
API -> Guard : requireOwner(token)
Guard -> Token : verify(token)
alt missing, invalid or expired token
  Token --> Guard : authentication error
  Guard --> API : authentication error
  API --> UI : 401; request ends
else verified signature and claims
  Token --> Guard : AccountId from subject
  Guard --> API : verified AccountId
  note right of API
    Use only the verified subject as owner.
    Continue with the feature service in S2-S7.
    That service validates its arguments and
    keeps repository queries scoped to this owner.
  end note
end
@enduml
